Subject: [PATCH] Trust configure for 128-bit types and popcount under MSVC

nauty.h overrode configure's answers whenever _MSC_VER was defined:
- it forced SIZEOF_UNINT128/SIZEOF_UINT128_T to 0, although configure had
  measured them, so with clang-cl (which has __int128) configure scheduled
  the WORDSIZE=128 libraries and they failed to compile;
- it used the _mm_popcnt intrinsics regardless of HAVE_HWPOPCNT, i.e. even
  with --disable-popcnt, emitting POPCNT on CPUs that may lack it.

Use the configured sizes, and the MSVC popcount intrinsics only when
configure enabled hardware popcount.
